{"kind":"artifact","text":"internal/app at merge 4f427f22acc2084dc282393318b47ade920ccc5c.\n\nAddActor no longer carries its own human/agent/service list; it asks workroom.IsActorKind, as does validateAuthorityRole. The accepted set and the error text are unchanged, and an omitted kind still defaults to agent.\n\nThe new test derives its expectation from the Workroom classifier instead of restating the three words, so adding a kind in one place and not the other fails. Verified by mutation rather than by a green suite: narrowing AddActor's accepted set fails it, and widening the vocabulary while AddActor keeps its own list fails it.\n\nThree live predecessors at these two paths are codex's — 22744290 at internal/workroom, and 9ba72fe1 and c935129e at internal/app — and I cannot retire them: decideSupersede admits a supersession only from the target's own author or a ratifier, with no exemption for naming a successor. I have retired the four that are mine. Saying so rather than leaving the paths looking settled.","body":{"commit":"4f427f22acc2084dc282393318b47ade920ccc5c","merge":"4f427f22acc2084dc282393318b47ade920ccc5c","path":"internal/app"}}